@startuml
title What one three-second oracle tick sets in motion
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F7FAFF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #4A78B5

start
:each validator computes its weighted
median of the included spot venues;
:validators publish; the clearinghouse takes
the stake-weighted median;
:recompute the mark price as the median
of its three candidate indices;
fork
  :re-evaluate account equity against
  maintenance margin, and start the
  liquidation ladder where it fails;<<#FDEEEE>>
fork again
  :check trigger orders: TP, SL,
  stop and take orders fire off mark;
fork again
  :restate unrealised PnL on every
  open position;
fork again
  :sample the funding premium from the
  impact bid and ask against the oracle;
  note right
    Sampled every 5 s and averaged over
    the hour. Payment settles hourly at
    one eighth of the 8 h rate, on the
    oracle price rather than the mark
  end note
fork again
  :revalue portfolio-margin collateral
  at the borrow oracle price, and run a
  borrow liquidation if a threshold is
  crossed;<<#FDEEEE>>
fork again
  :re-apply the order-entry bands: reject
  orders priced too far from the oracle,
  and aggressive orders at an OI cap;<<#FFF7E6>>
end fork
:next tick in about 3 seconds;
stop
@enduml
